## Findings

1. **High — Launch classification polling does not meet the required transient-tolerance contract.** In `.apnea/artifacts/plan.md:341`, `wait_non_shell_group` uses a 30-second deadline and immediately returns failure when `herdr pane process-info` fails, its foreground PGID cannot be parsed, or a non-shell sample temporarily lacks exactly one group-leader process. The dispatch requires every such transient sample—including Herdr failures, empty foreground lists, shell-only observations, and a temporarily missing group leader—to be retried until a 60-second deadline. Success must occur only when a non-shell PGID has exactly its group-leader host PID. Revise the function and both launch paths to retain/emit sample diagnostics while continuing on individual invalid samples.

